      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is not a bug-- this is how the Lipsync module works. It is not expected that the \"sil\" shape is what is triggered once speaking stops.\n\nPer the documentation on the lipsync module (https://developer.oculus.com/documentation/audiosdk/latest/concepts/book-audio-ovrlipsync/?locale=en_US), the \"silent\" blendshape is only used when the microphone is active but there's no active sound detected. When your microphone goes inactive, all of your viseme blendshapes are reset to zero.\n\nThis worked previously because of a bug in VRChat where the blendshapes were not reset properly when speaking completed. We have fixed this bug. Unfortunately, those relying on that previously broken behavior will need to update their avatars accordingly.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
