  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-31T21:46:39.249Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I use the sil blendshape to close the mouth of my models. With the recent VRChat update this functionality is removed. \n\nUnfortunately I sell my models on gumroad so now all of my users (~120) also have this problem.\n\nThe silence blendshape is very important to any workflow that involves baking normals, since you typically want the mouth open during baking. Leaving the mouth open in the basis shape is nice just in case I spot something that needs to be re-baked, it prevents me from having to re-open the mouth.\n\nThere should be no assumption that the basis shape is the same as the silence shape. I think the most straightforward thinking is that the silence blendshape would be active during silence!",
